sh translations","Terms with Ukrainian translations","en:Pathology"],"links":[["pathology","pathology"],["metabolic","metabolic"],["ketone","ketone"],["glycogen","glycogen"],["fasting","fasting"]],"raw_glosses":["(pathology) A metabolic state in which the body produces ketones to be used as fuel by some organs so that glycogen can be reserved for organs that depend on it. This condition occurs during times of fasting, starvation, or while on a ketogenic diet."],"glosses":["A metabolic state in which the body produces ketones to be used as fuel by some organs so that glycogen can be reserved for organs that depend on it. This condition occurs during times of fasting, starvation, or while on a ketogenic diet."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"9123d63c-bbe4-421b-a568-877e687159bc"}],"related":[{"word":"ketoacidosis"}],"synonyms":[]},"ketoacidosis":{"id":"f07ce617-f4e0-4bc1-a9ba-3fc1fa679751","word":"ketoacidosis","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"severe form of ketosis","tags":["feminine"],"word":"cetoacidose"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"topics":["biology","medicine","natural-sciences","sciences"],"categories":["English countable nouns","English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English nouns","English nouns with irregular plurals","English terms prefixed with keto-","English uncountable nouns","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Terms with Czech translations","Terms with Finnish translations","Terms with German translations","Terms with Hungarian translations","Terms with Irish translations","Terms with Mandarin translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","en:Biology","en:Medicine"],"links":[["biology","biology"],["medicine","medicine"],["ketosis","ketosis"],["diabetic","diabetic"],["ketone","ketone"],["acidosis","acidosis"]],"raw_glosses":["(biology, medicine) A severe form of ketosis, most commonly seen in diabetics, in which so much ketone is